# The case table of the 2026-10-18 ANSI spike
# (.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-18-phase-9d/spike-ansi-model.md). Each case is
# one operation: `infix OP | a | b`, `prefix OP | a`, `bif NAME | args`,
# `msg NAME | target | args` or `do count|for | n`. A field is a Rexx
# literal; an empty field is an omitted argument. The answer is the model's,
# untrapped and then under SIGNAL ON LOSTDIGITS: V[value], S code or
# L[description]. A `crate:` line is this crate's answer where it differs.

case name=add-wide-integer
infix + | 1111111111 | 0
